{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.88,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U1", "U8"],
      "pins": ["U1.4", "U1.5", "U8.4", "U8.5", "U1.8", "U8.8"],
      "nets": ["GND", "5V_switched_CAN", "NET0071"],
      "observed": "The isolated CAN transceivers U1 and U8 have both their primary-side ground (GND1) and secondary-side ground (GND2) connected to the common GND net. Their secondary supplies (VCC2) are connected to 5V_switched_CAN, which is a switched +5V rail referenced to the same GND rather than an isolated rail.",
      "expected": "For the specified isolated CAN buses, the transceiver secondary ground and secondary supply must be galvanically isolated from the primary side; GND1 and GND2 should not be merged, and VCC2 should be powered from an isolated supply.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\"))\n      (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\"))\n      (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"52\") (name \"5V_switched_CAN\") ... (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC2\") (pintype \"power_in\")) ... (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver"}
      ],
      "impact": "The intended galvanic isolation between the CM4/CAN-controller side and the external CAN bus is defeated. This creates ground-loop paths and removes the isolation protection that the design specification describes.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show a clear deviation from the intended isolated CAN architecture: isolated transceivers U1 and U8 have both GND1 and GND2 tied to common GND and VCC2 supplied from a non-isolated switched +5V rail, shorting out the isolation barrier."
}

